---
// /tool-coverage — Tool × Failure-Mode evidence heatmap.
// Loads /tool_fm_heatmap.json (produced by research/plot_tool_fm_heatmap.py).
// Cells are tiered 0..3; color encodes *per-mapping* evidence, never popularity.
// Rendered as an HTML table (accessible, SEO-visible, no chart library).
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
const title = "Tool × Failure-Mode Coverage";
---

<BaseLayout title={title}>
  <section class="mb-6 max-w-3xl">
    <p class="font-sans text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-faint">
      Coverage Matrix
    </p>
    <h1 class="mt-2">Tool × Failure-Mode evidence</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-7">
      Which of the supervision tools in the KG address which failure modes,
      and how strong is the evidence for each mapping? Cell color encodes an
      <strong>evidence tier for that specific (tool, failure-mode) pair</strong>
      — not tool popularity. GitHub stars, a crude popularity proxy, are
      relegated to the row labels; letting them drive color would paint a
      popular tool's whole row the same shade regardless of fit, which is the
      opposite of what this figure should surface.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-8 max-w-3xl">
    <h2 class="!mt-0 text-lg">Tiers</h2>
    <ul class="text-sm leading-7 space-y-1">
      <li><span class="inline-block w-4 h-4 align-middle rounded-sm border border-ink/15" style="background:#f5f5f5"></span>
        <strong>0</strong> — tool does not list this failure mode in <code>addresses_failure_modes</code>.</li>
      <li><span class="inline-block w-4 h-4 align-middle rounded-sm" style="background:#d8e7f5"></span>
        <strong>1 — declared mapping</strong>: the tool's YAML asserts it addresses this FM, but nothing more.</li>
      <li><span class="inline-block w-4 h-4 align-middle rounded-sm" style="background:#6aa3d3"></span>
        <strong>2 — rationale mentions it</strong>: the tool's <code>inclusion_rationale</code> actually discusses this FM
        (id, synonym, or phrase match). A per-mapping signal, not a per-tool one.</li>
      <li><span class="inline-block w-4 h-4 align-middle rounded-sm" style="background:#1f4e79"></span>
        <strong>3 — external citation</strong>: tier 2 plus the tool has a paper / dataset / documentation reference
        in <code>cited_in</code>, <code>documented_in</code>, or <code>evaluated_on</code>.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-4 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4 text-sm font-sans">
    <div>
      <label class="text-xs font-semibold text-ink-faint uppercase tracking-wide mr-2">Show</label>
      <select id="tc-scope" class="border border-ink/15 rounded px-2 py-1 bg-white">
        <option value="covering" selected>11 tools, every failure mode covered</option>
        <option value="top">Top 11 by coverage breadth</option>
        <option value="all">All tools with ≥1 mapping</option>
      </select>
    </div>
    <div class="text-xs text-ink-faint" id="tc-count"></div>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-8">
    <div class="overflow-x-auto border border-ink/10 rounded bg-white">
      <table class="text-sm font-sans w-full" id="tc-table">
        <thead class="bg-paper-alt text-ink-faint text-xs uppercase tracking-wide">
          <tr id="tc-head">
            <th class="text-left px-3 py-2 sticky left-0 bg-paper-alt">Tool</th>
            <th class="text-right px-3 py-2">Stars</th>
            <th class="text-right px-3 py-2">Breadth</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody id="tc-body">
          <tr><td colspan="3" class="px-3 py-6 text-center text-ink-faint">Loading…</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <noscript>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-faint">
        Raw data: <a href="/tool_fm_heatmap.json"><code>/tool_fm_heatmap.json</code></a>
      </p>
    </noscript>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-8 max-w-3xl">
    <h2>Three views, different questions</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-sm leading-7 space-y-1">
      <li><strong>"Every failure mode covered"</strong> (default) — greedy set cover picks the smallest set
        of tools whose combined declared coverage fills every column, then pads to 11 rows with the highest
        evidence-tier remaining tools. A dashed divider separates the specialists (above) from the depth pad
        (below). Answers: <em>"can the KG claim coverage of every failure mode at all?"</em></li>
      <li><strong>"Top by coverage breadth"</strong> — rank tools by how many FMs each declares. Dominated by
        evaluation harnesses (promptfoo, giskard, opik, phoenix, Guardrails, NeMo, logfire). Leaves
        specialist columns (obsolescence, dependency blindness) empty because narrow-but-deep tools get ranked
        out. Answers: <em>"what does the busy part of the map look like?"</em></li>
      <li><strong>"All tools with ≥1 mapping"</strong> — every tool that declares any FM. Useful when you're
        hunting for a specific tool (e.g. Context Hub, Semgrep, Renovate) that doesn't appear in the top
        views because its breadth is low.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="text-sm leading-7 mt-3">
      <strong>Almost every filled cell is tier 1 right now.</strong> Only a handful of tier-2 cells
      (rationales that explicitly name the FM they address), no tier-3 cells. This is the KG honestly
      admitting that it holds declarations more than evidence today — closing that gap is exactly what
      the citation / crosswalk pipeline is built to do.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-10 max-w-3xl">
    <h2>Methodology notes</h2>
    <p class="text-sm leading-7">
      Tools are ranked by <code>breadth</code> (count of failure modes declared), ties broken by
      <code>tier_sum</code> (row evidence total) and then by stars. Columns are ordered by how many of the
      top-N tools address each failure mode, so "most-covered" failure modes sit on the left.
      The per-mapping <strong>rationale match</strong> (tier 2) uses a conservative keyword set per failure mode,
      kept intentionally narrow because false positives here silently inflate evidence.
    </p>
    <p class="text-sm leading-7 mt-3">
      Reproduce with <code>.venv/bin/python research/plot_tool_fm_heatmap.py</code>.
      Outputs live under <code>research/figures/</code> (static PNG/PDF for the paper) and
      <code>site/public/tool_fm_heatmap.json</code> (data for this page).
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<script>
  type Tier = 0 | 1 | 2 | 3;

  interface ToolRow {
    id: string;
    name: string;
    stars: number;
    trending?: boolean;
    breadth: number;
    tier_sum: number;
    tiers: Record<string, number>;
  }

  interface Payload {
    top_n: number;
    failure_modes: string[];
    failure_mode_display: Record<string, string>;
    tools_top: ToolRow[];
    tools_covering: ToolRow[];
    tools_all: ToolRow[];
    covering_divider?: number;
    legend: Record<string, string>;
    selections?: Record<string, string>;
  }

  const TIER_BG: Record<number, string> = {
    0: "#f5f5f5",
    1: "#d8e7f5",
    2: "#6aa3d3",
    3: "#1f4e79",
  };
  const TIER_FG: Record<number, string> = {
    0: "#9ca3af",
    1: "#1f4e79",
    2: "#ffffff",
    3: "#ffffff",
  };
  const TIER_LABEL: Record<number, string> = {
    0: "not addressed",
    1: "declared mapping",
    2: "rationale discusses FM",
    3: "rationale + external citation",
  };

  const TABLE = document.getElementById("tc-table") as HTMLTableElement | null;
  const HEAD = document.getElementById("tc-head") as HTMLTableRowElement | null;
  const BODY = document.getElementById("tc-body") as HTMLTableSectionElement | null;
  const COUNT = document.getElementById("tc-count") as HTMLElement | null;
  const SCOPE = document.getElementById("tc-scope") as HTMLSelectElement | null;

  let payload: Payload | null = null;

  function escapeHtml(s: string): string {
    return s.replace(/&/g, "&amp;").replace(/</g, "&lt;")
      .replace(/>/g, "&gt;").replace(/"/g, "&quot;");
  }

  function fmtStars(n: number): string {
    if (!n) return "—";
    if (n >= 1000) return `${(n / 1000).toFixed(1)}k`;
    return String(n);
  }

  function render(): void {
    if (!payload || !HEAD || !BODY || !COUNT || !SCOPE) return;
    const scopeKey = SCOPE.value;
    const scopeToField: Record<string, keyof Payload> = {
      covering: "tools_covering",
      top: "tools_top",
      all: "tools_all",
    };
    const field = scopeToField[scopeKey] ?? "tools_covering";
    const rowsRaw = (payload[field] as unknown as ToolRow[]) ?? [];
    const rows = scopeKey === "all"
      ? rowsRaw.filter((r) => r.breadth > 0)
      : rowsRaw;
    const divider = scopeKey === "covering" ? (payload.covering_divider ?? 0) : 0;

    // head
    HEAD.innerHTML =
      `<th class="text-left px-3 py-2 sticky left-0 bg-paper-alt z-10">Tool</th>`
      + `<th class="text-right px-3 py-2">Stars</th>`
      + `<th class="text-right px-3 py-2">Breadth</th>`
      + payload.failure_modes.map((fm) => {
        const disp = payload!.failure_mode_display[fm] ?? fm;
        return `<th class="px-2 py-2 align-bottom" style="min-width:3rem">`
          + `<a href="/failure-modes/${encodeURIComponent(fm)}" class="block text-ink hover:text-accent"`
          + ` title="${escapeHtml(disp)}">`
          + `<div style="writing-mode: vertical-rl; transform: rotate(180deg); white-space: nowrap;"`
          + ` class="text-xs normal-case tracking-normal">${escapeHtml(disp)}</div></a></th>`;
      }).join("");

    // body
    BODY.innerHTML = rows.map((r, rowIdx) => {
      const isLastSpecialist = divider > 0 && rowIdx === divider - 1;
      const dividerCls = isLastSpecialist ? " border-b-2 border-dashed border-[#1f4e79]" : "";
      const cells = payload!.failure_modes.map((fm) => {
        const t = (r.tiers[fm] ?? 0) as Tier;
        const bg = TIER_BG[t];
        const fg = TIER_FG[t];
        const tip = `${r.name} × ${payload!.failure_mode_display[fm]}: tier ${t} — ${TIER_LABEL[t]}`;
        const content = t === 0 ? "" : String(t);
        const clickable = t > 0
          ? `<a href="/tools/${encodeURIComponent(r.id)}" title="${escapeHtml(tip)}"`
            + ` class="block w-full h-full no-underline leading-none"`
            + ` style="color:${fg}">${content}</a>`
          : `<span title="${escapeHtml(tip)}" class="block w-full h-full">&nbsp;</span>`;
        return `<td class="text-center align-middle p-0" style="background:${bg}; height:2.25rem; min-width:2.25rem">`
          + clickable + `</td>`;
      }).join("");
      const trendingMark = r.trending
        ? ` <span class="ml-1" title="On github.com/trending — rank tiebreak preferred">🔥</span>`
        : "";
      return `<tr class="border-t border-ink/10${dividerCls}">`
        + `<td class="px-3 py-1.5 sticky left-0 bg-white z-10 border-r border-ink/10">`
        + `<a href="/tools/${encodeURIComponent(r.id)}" class="text-ink hover:text-accent">${escapeHtml(r.name)}</a>${trendingMark}`
        + `</td>`
        + `<td class="px-3 py-1.5 text-right font-mono text-xs text-ink-muted">${fmtStars(r.stars)}</td>`
        + `<td class="px-3 py-1.5 text-right font-mono text-xs">${r.breadth}</td>`
        + cells + `</tr>`;
    }).join("");

    let countText = `${rows.length} tool${rows.length === 1 ? "" : "s"} shown`
      + ` · ${payload.failure_modes.length} failure modes`;
    if (scopeKey === "covering" && divider > 0) {
      countText += ` · ${divider} specialist${divider === 1 ? "" : "s"} cover every FM; rows below pad for depth`;
    }
    COUNT.textContent = countText;
  }

  async function init(): Promise<void> {
    try {
      const res = await fetch("/tool_fm_heatmap.json");
      if (!res.ok) throw new Error(`HTTP ${res.status}`);
      payload = (await res.json()) as Payload;
    } catch (err) {
      if (BODY) {
        BODY.innerHTML = `<tr><td colspan="3" class="px-3 py-6 text-center text-ink-faint">`
          + `Failed to load /tool_fm_heatmap.json (${escapeHtml(String(err))}). `
          + `Run: .venv/bin/python research/plot_tool_fm_heatmap.py</td></tr>`;
      }
      return;
    }
    render();
    SCOPE?.addEventListener("change", render);
  }

  init();
</script>
